      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a stronger revision that emphasizes the right to choose and the breakdown of trust.\n\n\"I must firmly object to the unilateral push for this new sex education curriculum, as it deeply undermines the fundamental right of parents to direct the moral and ethical education of their own children. When the school district proceeds to bypass the clear authority of the home on such sensitive topics, it is an unacceptable breach of the trust essential to the partnership between the community and the district. I believe the institution should never claim the moral authority to legislate deeply personal values, and I demand that this decision be subject to direct and decisive community and parental approval first. \"",
      "source": "target",
